<title>FRANCE: French co-ops say EU must rethink grain mkt policy.</title>
<headline>French co-ops say EU must rethink grain mkt policy.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union must rethink the organisation of its grain markets or lose export markets to more competitive suppliers, the French grain cooperatives federation FFCAT said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;If the European Union wants to maintain its position (as a key exporter), it must adapt,&quot; FFCAT deputy director general Christian Duval told a news conference.</p>
<p>Faced with record crops at home and tough competition on world markets, EU producers need less restrictive rules to operate, FFCAT officials said.</p>
</text>
